WEBVTT

NOTE Authored baseline guidance. Offline synthetic Flite slt narration. Sentence-segment timing measured from actual WAV files; not phoneme alignment.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
Authored guidance with offline synthetic narration.

2
00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.085
Connect two stages.

3
00:00:05.335 --> 00:00:09.400
The front gear has 40 teeth and turns at 30
revolutions per minute.

4
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.680
Each full turn advances 40 chain pitches.

5
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:17.235
The ideal no-slip chain carries the same chain
pitches past both gears.

6
00:00:17.485 --> 00:00:20.315
Take apart pauses motion for inspection.

7
00:00:20.565 --> 00:00:24.610
Cancel restores the entry view; Put back restores
the assembly.

8
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:27.555
Pulling does not disconnect the model.

9
00:00:27.805 --> 00:00:32.080
Stage 1 rear and stage 2 front share 60 revolutions
per minute.

10
00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:39.010
Stage 2 uses 32/16 teeth, so its rear output is 120
revolutions per minute.

11
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.830
Only the independent first-stage cadence is
editable.

12
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.730
Shaft spacing and depth are schematic.

